 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "TimeMeasure.lean only provides `timeMeasure_Ioc`, `timeMeasure_univ`, `timeMeasure_zero`, `timeMeasure_singleton_zero` and `timeMeasure_restrict`, and each proof unfolds `timeMeasure_def` itself. RandomMatrices/README.md:1185: 'finite horizons measured by its `timeMeasure T`; collision and exit times are\u2026'.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Probability/Process/TimeMeasure.lean",
   "fix": "Add `timeMeasure_apply (T) {s : Set \u211d\u22650} (hs : MeasurableSet s) : timeMeasure T s = volume (((\u2191) : \u211d\u22650 \u2192 \u211d) '' (s \u2229 Ioc 0 T))`, proved with `Measure.restrict_apply` and `MeasurableEmbedding.comap_apply`, and derive `timeMeasure_Ioc` and `timeMeasure_singleton_zero` from it.",
   "issue": "`timeMeasure` has no general apply lemma. Mass of any measurable set other than `Ioc s t`, `univ` or `{0}` (e.g. `Icc`, `Ioo`, `{t}` with `t \u2260 0`, or a.e. sets) can only be computed by unfolding `timeMeasure_def` and working through the comap/restrict API. That blocks unfold-free use, including the RandomMatrices consumers that measure collision and exit times with `timeMeasure T`.",
   "line": 31
  }
 ],
